  "vendor_schema": "aps.athena_summary",
  "payload": {
   "provider": "Dr. David Ortiz",
   "specialty": "cardiology",
   "page_count": 2,
   "pages": [
    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "FAX 14  CONFIDENTIAL\nCLINICAL SUMMARY - Farrell Miller and Adams Medical Group\n\nPatient: Tracy Patterson\nDOB: 09/08/1945\nSex: F\nMRN: 871429\n\n**Encounters:**\n\n2025-04-26\n- **Reason for Visit:** Heart failure / cardiomyopathy\n- **Blood Pressure:** 114/84\n- **Weight:** 137 lbs\n\n2024-01-22\n- **Reason for Visit:** Heart failure / cardiomyopathy\n- **Blood Pressure:** 108/85\n- **Weight:** 134 lbs\n\n2022-10-18\n- **Reason for Visit:** Heart failure / cardiomyopathy\n- **Blood Pressure:** 118/90\n- **Weight:** 138 lbs\n\n---\n\n**Assessment/Plan:**\n\n- **Heart Failure / Cardiomyopathy (EF 53%; recovered ~4.8 years):** The patient's heart failure, diagnosed in August 2021, is currently well-controlled. She has been managing her condition with a combination of medications including spironolactone 50 mg and empagliflozin 25 mg. Her ejection fraction (EF) remains at 53%. The patient has been symptom-free for approximately 4.8 years.\n \n- **Medications:**\n - **Spironolactone 50 mg:** One tablet daily to manage heart failure and prevent potassium loss.\n - **Empagliflozin 25 mg:** One tablet daily for improving heart failure outcomes and blood sugar control.\n \n- **Vital Signs and Weight Monitoring:** The patient's vital signs and weight have been monitored. Her blood pressure has remained within acceptable limits during the recent visits. Weight has been stable, with a slight fluctuation from 134 lbs to 137 lbs last year.\n\n- **Exercise:** The patient engages in regular physical activity, running 3-4 times a week, which helps in maintaining her cardiovascular health.\n\n- **Social History:**\n - **Tobacco Use:** The patient is a former smoker, having smoked approximately half a pack per day. She quit smoking in March 2018. Her disclosure regarding tobacco use has been honest and consistent.\n - **Alcohol Consumption:** The patient reports no alcohol consumption.\n\n**Additional Findings:**\n\n- **Physical Examination:** On recent evaluations, the patient's physical exam has shown no signs of fluid overload, and her heart are normal without any murmurs. Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally, and there is no peripheral edema.\n \n- **Routine Lab Work:** Recent lab tests have shown stable renal function and electrolytes within normal limits. Her liver function tests have also remained normal.\n\n**Miscellaneous:**\n\n- **Patient Complaints:** The patient reports occasional mild dizziness, which she attributes to minor orthostatic changes and not to her cardiac condition. She also mentioned experiencing mild fatigue, which she has been managing well with her current regimen.\n\n- **Ad"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "ministrative Notes:** The patient has been compliant with all follow-up appointments and has shown a good understanding of her condition and medication regimen. There are no outstanding issues related to her care.\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nTracy Patterson's heart failure and cardiomyopathy are well-managed with her current medical therapy. Her ejection fraction remains stable, and she continues to be symptom-free for over 4.8 years. Regular monitoring and adherence to her medication regimen are key to maintaining her current health status. The patient’s commitment to a healthy lifestyle, including regular exercise, has contributed to the control of her condition.\n\n---\n\n**Dr. David Ortiz** \nCardiology \nFarrell Miller and Adams Medical Group\n"
    }
   ],
